{% extends 'pages/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan-layout.html.twig' %}
{% set plan_key = 'government' %}{% set plan_short = 'Member government' %}{% set plan_eyebrow = 'Priority 1' %}
{% set plan_title = 'Member power and open government' %}
{% set plan_description = 'Move authority toward members by making records, decisions, meetings, conflicts and appeals visible before trust is lost.' %}
{% block plan_content %}
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">The outcome</p><h2>Members can see a decision, understand it, challenge it and change the rules.</h2><p class="plan-lede">Government becomes predictable. Members know where a decision is made, what information supported it, who participated and how to seek review.</p></header><div class="plan-grid plan-grid--3"><div class="plan-card"><h3>Open by default</h3><p>Budgets, policies, agendas, minutes, resolutions and major agreements follow a publication schedule.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Reasons on the record</h3><p>Major decisions state the authority, options, cost, conflicts, vote and expected member benefit.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>A real appeal path</h3><p>Members can challenge a refusal, missed deadline or process failure outside the office that made it.</p></div></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Year One commitments</p><h2>Build the machinery of member oversight.</h2></header><div class="plan-commitments"><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Member records law</h3><p>Define accessible records, privacy limits, response times, fees, redaction reasons and independent appeal.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Decision register</h3><p>Publish every open-session motion and resolution with status, cost, accountable office and supporting record.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Meetings members can follow</h3><p>Publish an annual calendar, agendas before meetings and approved minutes on a fixed deadline.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Conflict system</h3><p>Publish the policy, annual disclosures for public roles, recusals and the process used to decide conflicts.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Member questions tracker</h3><p>Record questions, responsible offices, due dates, answers and overdue items without exposing member PII.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Member lawmaking path</h3><p>Set clear routes for member petitions, resolutions, law proposals, referendums and recall.</p></article></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Quarterly measures</p><h2>What members receive.</h2></header><div class="plan-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Measure</th><th>First baseline</th><th>Year One direction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Records requests answered within standard</td><td>Publish total, response time and outcome</td><td>Increase on-time completion each quarter</td></tr><tr><td>Open decisions posted with reasons</td><td>Count all eligible decisions</td><td>100% posted within the adopted deadline</td></tr><tr><td>Scheduled minutes posted</td><td>Publication lag by meeting</td><td>No unexplained backlog</td></tr><tr><td>Appeals received and resolved</td><td>Establish the first public count</td><td>Every appeal receives a written decision</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="plan-decision"><h2>Decisions members make</h2><ul><li>Which records must always be public?</li><li>Who appoints the independent appeal body?</li><li>What signature threshold starts a member resolution or recall vote?</li><li>Which major decisions require consultation or direct member approval?</li></ul></section>
